PrepFlow
API Design Document

Version: v1.0

Status: Draft

Author: Tejas Nere

1. Purpose

This document defines all backend APIs required for PrepFlow.

The API architecture follows REST principles and provides a consistent communication layer between the frontend and backend.

Every response should follow a standardized structure.

2. API Principles

Every API should:

Follow REST standards
Return meaningful responses
Validate input
Handle errors gracefully
Use consistent naming conventions
Support future scalability
3. Response Structure

Every successful API should return:

{
    "success": true,
    "message": "",
    "data": {}
}

Every failed API should return:

{
    "success": false,
    "message": "",
    "error": {}
}
4. Authentication APIs
Login

POST

/api/auth/login

Purpose

Administrator Login

Logout

POST

/api/auth/logout

Purpose

Logout Current User

Current User

GET

/api/auth/me

Purpose

Return Logged In User Information

