20. Authorization Rules

Student

Can

View Subjects
View Chapters
View Resources
Update Own Progress

Cannot

Create
Edit
Delete Platform Content

Administrator

Can Access

Every API

21. Status Codes

200

Success

201

Created

400

Bad Request

401

Unauthorized

403

Forbidden

404

Not Found

500

Internal Server Error

22. Validation Rules

Every API should validate:

Required Fields

Invalid IDs

File Types

Permissions

Duplicate Entries

No invalid request should reach the database.

23. Error Messages

Errors should always be meaningful.

Examples

Subject Not Found

Invalid Resource

Unauthorized Access

Upload Failed

Chapter Already Exists

24. Security

Protected APIs require authentication.

Admin APIs require administrator role.

Tokens should never expose sensitive information.

25. API Design Principles

RESTful

Simple

Consistent

Scalable

Secure

Reusable

26. Future Scalability

The API architecture should support future features without breaking existing endpoints.

New modules should be added without modifying previous APIs.

27. Final Statement

PrepFlow APIs are designed to provide a clean, scalable, and maintainable communication layer between the frontend, backend, database, and storage systems.

Every endpoint should remain modular, reusable, and future-ready.